00:35:30.484 --> 00:35:34.310
in the studio, everyone has to evacuate.

00:35:34.310 --> 00:35:36.210
You don't have to eat it, you
just have to get close to it.

00:35:36.210 --> 00:35:38.330
- We didn't even attempt to taste it,

00:35:38.330 --> 00:35:40.863
but if we opened it
now, I bet you we would.

00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.667
And I think that's what I wanna get at.

00:35:43.667 --> 00:35:46.280
- But I wouldn't enjoy it.

00:35:46.280 --> 00:35:48.498
I'm gonna do it.

00:35:48.498 --> 00:35:51.410
I'm gonna do it because it's
the spirit of our show is

00:35:51.410 --> 00:35:54.810
to try things and, but I'm
not trying it thinking,

00:35:54.810 --> 00:35:56.900
you know what, I might like this,

00:35:56.900 --> 00:35:59.900
even that's kind of the unspoken premise

00:35:59.900 --> 00:36:01.240
or sometimes the spoken premise

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:03.750
of our show is Will It whatever is like,

00:36:03.750 --> 00:36:06.470
is this gonna be unexpectedly
good but I don't go

00:36:06.470 --> 00:36:08.570
into those situations
thinking the way that I think

00:36:08.570 --> 00:36:12.990
about like okay sushi is an example.

00:36:12.990 --> 00:36:14.450
We didn't grow up eating sushi.

00:36:14.450 --> 00:36:16.190
A lot of people our age
didn't grow up eating sushi

00:36:16.190 --> 00:36:17.800
but especially where we're from.

00:36:17.800 --> 00:36:21.440
So the first time I ever
had sushi, it was weird.

00:36:21.440 --> 00:36:23.650
The wasabi was a completely new taste,

00:36:23.650 --> 00:36:26.880
the eating ginger was, all
that was completely new

00:36:26.880 --> 00:36:31.337
and exotic and I didn't
really like it the first time

00:36:31.337 --> 00:36:33.240
and then kinda liked it the second time

00:36:33.240 --> 00:36:35.262
and then third, fourth
time I was in and now,

00:36:35.262 --> 00:36:38.142
I can actually find
myself craving it, right?

00:36:38.142 --> 00:36:40.227
But--
- And I think that--

00:36:41.180 --> 00:36:42.313
- I just don't see what we do.

00:36:42.313 --> 00:36:44.960
- I don't know if that's benign masochism.

00:36:44.960 --> 00:36:48.720
I do think that there is
acquiring a taste for something

00:36:48.720 --> 00:36:51.302
through another means
that isn't the pleasure

00:36:51.302 --> 00:36:54.210
of feeling like you're
going to harm yourself

00:36:54.210 --> 00:36:55.110
but you're not.

00:36:55.110 --> 00:36:56.630
I think there are other routes

00:36:56.630 --> 00:37:01.496
to changing your mind
over time about something.

00:37:01.496 --> 00:37:06.496
But I would like to look
back, I kinda, like I said,

00:37:07.410 --> 00:37:09.380
I traced Good Mythical Morning,

00:37:09.380 --> 00:37:10.730
how did we get to a point

00:37:10.730 --> 00:37:12.476
where we started eating so much food?

00:37:12.476 --> 00:37:17.476
And, it's interesting that it hasn't,

00:37:18.053 --> 00:37:21.234
what you said is that
there's not a component

00:37:21.234 --> 00:37:26.150
of it that we actually enjoyed.

00:37:26.150 --> 00:37:28.800
We don't actually enjoy in
the moment eating this stuff

00:37:28.800 --> 00:37:31.090
that we're gagging,
that's why we gag it out.

00:37:31.090 --> 00:37:33.159
But--
- I enjoy every

00:37:33.159 --> 00:37:35.400
other aspect of it.
- I enjoy every

00:37:35.400 --> 00:37:36.233
other aspect of it.

00:37:36.233 --> 00:37:38.040
- So don't feel sorry for us.
- Don't feel sorry.

00:37:38.040 --> 00:37:40.190
- Don't make comments
where you say things like,

00:37:40.190 --> 00:37:42.900
if you guys don't enjoy it, don't do it.

00:37:42.900 --> 00:37:45.410
- We enjoy--
- Most people do enjoy

00:37:45.410 --> 00:37:47.610
watching us not enjoy it so. (chuckles)

00:37:47.610 --> 00:37:49.570
- And we enjoy--
- We gon' keep doing it.

00:37:49.570 --> 00:37:54.510
- We enjoy our audience enjoying
that we're not enjoying it

00:37:54.510 --> 00:37:55.910
and that makes us enjoy it.

00:37:55.910 --> 00:37:59.600
- And when I watch those
montages of us trying

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:01.938
to get things down and not being able to,

00:38:01.938 --> 00:38:04.920
I mean, you've seen the
that I react in the moment

00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:06.730
when you can't get something down, I mean,

00:38:06.730 --> 00:38:09.901
it brings me joy.
(Link chuckles)

00:38:09.901 --> 00:38:14.800
There is pure joy in
watching your best friend

00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:16.708
not be able to get food down.

00:38:16.708 --> 00:38:19.420
That's great, there's
a lot of joy in that.

00:38:19.420 --> 00:38:24.050
- I was surprised at how
we got to this point,

00:38:24.050 --> 00:38:27.076
so, perhaps there's a digression.

00:38:27.076 --> 00:38:30.212
I just wanted to take us
down memory lane because

00:38:30.212 --> 00:38:34.470
I always tend to think
of Will It as, you know,

00:38:34.470 --> 00:38:37.623
we did an episode called Will It Taco.

00:38:43.160 --> 00:38:45.510
(Rhett gags)
(crew laughs)

00:38:45.510 --> 00:38:50.510
We did that episode on
Cinco de Mayo of 2014.

00:38:51.950 --> 00:38:53.590
- Okay.

00:38:53.590 --> 00:38:54.743
Almost five years ago.

00:38:55.760 --> 00:38:57.140
- And I went back and
I watched part of that.

00:38:57.140 --> 00:39:00.264
Used hard shells, we just put stuff in it.

00:39:00.264 --> 00:39:01.963
Broccoli and cheese.

00:39:03.700 --> 00:39:07.920
I made a comment on that episode
before we ate pork blood,

00:39:07.920 --> 00:39:12.286
congealed pork blood in little
cube, long cube logs of it,

00:39:12.286 --> 00:39:14.447
I said, "This is why
we're on the internet.

00:39:14.447 --> 00:39:16.190
"This is our destiny."

00:39:16.190 --> 00:39:18.090
Like I said that.
- You're a prophet.

00:39:19.539 --> 00:39:21.380
- Which is really, really stupid.

00:39:21.380 --> 00:39:22.803
I shouldn't have said
that but I tend to think

00:39:22.803 --> 00:39:25.630
that that's the moment
where this thing started

00:39:25.630 --> 00:39:27.713
to careen into crazy.

00:39:29.483 --> 00:39:33.270
That was season five, episode 82.

00:39:33.270 --> 00:39:34.760
So I went all the way
back to the beginning,

00:39:34.760 --> 00:39:36.190
it's like when did we
really start eating stuff?

00:39:36.190 --> 00:39:39.611
Season one episode five
we did Best Candy Bar Ever

00:39:39.611 --> 00:39:43.076
and then maybe a month or two
later we did Best Cereal Ever.

00:39:43.076 --> 00:39:45.076
We were trying different best evers

00:39:45.076 --> 00:39:47.520
and we were doing toys
and all types of stuff.

00:39:47.520 --> 00:39:50.010
It didn't catch, so even
though very early on,

00:39:50.010 --> 00:39:52.371
we did eat some stuff and rank it,

00:39:52.371 --> 00:39:55.056
which we came full circle on that.

00:39:55.056 --> 00:39:55.889
- Right.

00:39:56.730 --> 00:39:58.160
- We abandoned it.

00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:00.930
That's all we did, those
two things in season one.

00:40:00.930 --> 00:40:03.700
Season one episode 76 was the next time

00:40:03.700 --> 00:40:05.350
I could find us eating something.

00:40:06.276 --> 00:40:09.940
They discontinued Twinkies
and we said we acquired one

00:40:09.940 --> 00:40:11.647
and I had never eaten a Twinkie.

00:40:11.647 --> 00:40:14.660
- How old was that Twinkie?
- The last Twinkie on earth.

00:40:14.660 --> 00:40:18.490
It was a fresh Twinkie but
the company was gonna go over.

00:40:18.490 --> 00:40:20.400
It was rescued and Twinkie still exists.

00:40:20.400 --> 00:40:22.403
- Or go under even.
- Yeah.

00:40:22.403 --> 00:40:24.170
It's the only thing we ate in season two.

00:40:24.170 --> 00:40:27.730
Season three episode
29, I was playing a game

00:40:27.730 --> 00:40:29.848
with you about ways to extend your life

00:40:29.848 --> 00:40:32.500
and every time you got a question right,

00:40:32.500 --> 00:40:36.200
I let you take a bite out
of a quadruple Whopper.

00:40:36.200 --> 00:40:37.410
- Oh man.
- Just 'cause I thought

00:40:37.410 --> 00:40:39.080
that would be funny.
- We had the good ideas

00:40:39.080 --> 00:40:40.410
back then didn't we?

00:40:40.410 --> 00:40:44.400
- Well we didn't know what
was happening, I mean--

00:40:44.400 --> 00:40:45.890
- I just wanted to eat
a quadruple Whopper.

00:40:45.890 --> 00:40:47.450
- And you loved it.
- Oh yeah.

00:40:47.450 --> 00:40:49.660
- You were eating this, you
would get a question right,

00:40:49.660 --> 00:40:51.450
you would just chomp on
this quadruple Whopper

00:40:51.450 --> 00:40:53.683
and it was a great thumbnail too.

00:40:54.640 --> 00:40:58.430
Of course, that didn't
really click into place.

00:40:58.430 --> 00:41:01.670
The only other thing
we ate in season three,

00:41:01.670 --> 00:41:06.400
there's an episode called
Rhett and Link Eat Insects.

00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:07.990
And I think that was,
I didn't watch that one

00:41:07.990 --> 00:41:10.610
but I think it's probably
like fans sending us

00:41:10.610 --> 00:41:12.660
crickets in a bag or something.

00:41:12.660 --> 00:41:14.749
I honestly didn't watch it.

00:41:14.749 --> 00:41:16.560
That's the only thing
we ate in season three,

00:41:16.560 --> 00:41:19.250
then we made The Mythical
Show and then we came back

00:41:19.250 --> 00:41:20.920
in season four--
- No food on

00:41:20.920 --> 00:41:22.210
The Mythical Show.

00:41:22.210 --> 00:41:23.710
- Not that I recall.

00:41:23.710 --> 00:41:26.351
- Interesting that we had not yet--

00:41:26.351 --> 00:41:28.423
- Understood--
- That definitely shows

00:41:28.423 --> 00:41:30.700
that we didn't understand the potential

00:41:30.700 --> 00:41:32.470
that there was in eating on camera,

00:41:32.470 --> 00:41:33.820
the fact that we created this show

00:41:33.820 --> 00:41:38.300
that we had such high hopes
for and didn't eat a thing.

00:41:38.300 --> 00:41:40.360
- Now.
- Maybe we did.

00:41:40.360 --> 00:41:42.034
- Now Will It Taco again was season five

00:41:42.034 --> 00:41:44.840
but I'm just starting season four.

00:41:44.840 --> 00:41:47.110
Everything that I could
find in the cursory search

00:41:47.110 --> 00:41:49.200
that we ate, I'm sure
there's a little bit more

00:41:49.200 --> 00:41:50.470
but not a whole lot.

00:41:50.470 --> 00:41:53.410
We did a thing called the
Habanero Pepper Challenge.

00:41:53.410 --> 00:41:56.030
I think that's where we ate
increasingly hot peppers,

00:41:56.030 --> 00:41:58.170
getting up to the habanero.

00:41:58.170 --> 00:41:59.953
That's before Hot Ones existed.

00:42:01.410 --> 00:42:04.459
We did that once, then
we did something called

00:42:04.459 --> 00:42:08.918
The Nooodle Showdown in season four

00:42:08.918 --> 00:42:12.920
where we ranked different
types of noodles,

00:42:12.920 --> 00:42:15.720
like in a tournament style.

00:42:15.720 --> 00:42:17.293
Then we never did that again.

00:42:18.501 --> 00:42:20.869
It's so fascinating to
me that we did this,

00:42:20.869 --> 00:42:23.200
why would we wanna taste noodles?

00:42:23.200 --> 00:42:24.950
- Oh, at that point we were really,

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:27.320
we were already trying to figure out--

00:42:27.320 --> 00:42:29.875
- We were out of ideas.
- What to do, yeah.

00:42:29.875 --> 00:42:33.170
- We got that pill, the
taste tripping pill.

00:42:33.170 --> 00:42:34.470
- Yeah.
- Where it makes sweet things

00:42:34.470 --> 00:42:35.520
sour and sour things sweet

00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:37.170
'cause we were big on experiments.

00:42:37.170 --> 00:42:38.930
Like that's how we thought of our show.

00:42:38.930 --> 00:42:41.042
We're not really eating
things, we only eat things

00:42:41.042 --> 00:42:44.000
if it's part of an experiment
or for inventing something

00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:47.043
'cause we invented the Big Mac and cheese

00:42:47.043 --> 00:42:49.673
and putting orange chicken on a sub.

00:42:50.920 --> 00:42:52.160
- That seems more recent.

00:42:52.160 --> 00:42:53.860
- No, season four.
- Season four?

00:42:53.860 --> 00:42:56.070
- Then we ate the ghost
pepper to follow up

00:42:56.070 --> 00:42:59.249
with the habanero challenge,
we did a ghost pepper episode.

00:42:59.249 --> 00:43:02.760
And then we did one called
The Strangest Candy on Earth.

00:43:02.760 --> 00:43:04.880
We just got international
candies and we just tasted them

00:43:04.880 --> 00:43:06.624
and talked about it.

00:43:06.624 --> 00:43:09.310
I mean out of all those
episodes of season four,

00:43:09.310 --> 00:43:10.930
those are all the ones
that are food-based.

00:43:10.930 --> 00:43:11.763
That's it.

00:43:12.833 --> 00:43:15.160
That's all I could find.

00:43:15.160 --> 00:43:19.167
Season five, we started
to get going a little bit.

00:43:19.167 --> 00:43:22.500
We tasted fake bacon.
- Mm-hmm.

00:43:22.500 --> 00:43:24.810
- And then a few episodes later

00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:27.079
we did an exotic meat taste test

00:43:27.079 --> 00:43:31.881
and then we started putting
sriracha on stuff and eating it.

00:43:31.881 --> 00:43:35.610
We got some of that cat
poof coffee and tried that.

00:43:35.610 --> 00:43:38.050
I said cat poof but it was cat poop.

00:43:38.050 --> 00:43:39.000
- Yeah it made it sound better.

00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:43.060
- We did a blind berry taste
test with Strawburry17.

00:43:43.060 --> 00:43:44.640
Again, this is an exhaustive list,

00:43:44.640 --> 00:43:45.730
this is not just highlights.

00:43:45.730 --> 00:43:47.630
These are the only food things we did.

00:43:48.477 --> 00:43:53.477
Then we did Bug War which
was me eating a scorpion.

00:43:53.810 --> 00:43:55.090
- Oh wow.

00:43:55.090 --> 00:43:55.923
That got a lot of clicks.

00:43:55.923 --> 00:43:58.420
- Season five, episode 57.

00:43:58.420 --> 00:44:00.440
That's like, became our
most-viewed video of all time

00:44:00.440 --> 00:44:03.180
because it was a thumbnail
of me holding up a scorpion

00:44:03.180 --> 00:44:06.210
and I actually ate the
whole frickin' thing.

00:44:06.210 --> 00:44:07.660
- Golly.
- But you see what got us

00:44:07.660 --> 00:44:09.970
to that point is, oh we ate
some bugs the previous season,

00:44:09.970 --> 00:44:11.911
we ate some exotic meats.

00:44:11.911 --> 00:44:13.533
Then we did a pizza taste.

00:44:14.413 --> 00:44:17.003
We just did that out of nowhere.

00:44:17.912 --> 00:44:21.280
I mean, I'm sure Buzzfeed
was doing their stuff too

00:44:21.280 --> 00:44:23.530
and there was a lot of
feeling like we're getting

00:44:23.530 --> 00:44:25.650
on each other's bandwagon or something.

00:44:25.650 --> 00:44:28.210
That was starting to happen.
- I don't know if we were,

00:44:28.210 --> 00:44:31.070
you think we were on the radar
at that point, that season?

00:44:31.070 --> 00:44:32.550
Maybe, I don't know.

00:44:32.550 --> 00:44:36.254
- Season five is when GMM
started taking off I think.

00:44:36.254 --> 00:44:38.366
We ate 40 year old ham and eggs

00:44:38.366 --> 00:44:41.470
and then we did Will It Taco.

00:44:41.470 --> 00:44:43.720
Then after that, in season five,

00:44:43.720 --> 00:44:46.170
we only did two more food
episodes I could find

00:44:46.170 --> 00:44:47.160
after Will It Taco.

00:44:47.160 --> 00:44:50.360
We did Flying Waffle, which
was Unidentified Flying Waffle,

00:44:50.360 --> 00:44:53.560
we tried to invent other
dishes like we did Big Mac

00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:54.980
and cheese the last season

00:44:54.980 --> 00:44:56.940
and that didn't work so we abandoned that.

00:44:56.940 --> 00:44:59.379
And then we did the
Squeezable Food Taste Test

00:44:59.379 --> 00:45:01.600
where we fired food at each other's faces.

00:45:01.600 --> 00:45:03.115
- Oh yeah yeah.
- Which was a lot of fun

00:45:03.115 --> 00:45:05.980
but that was just a weird
one-off 'cause we were doing

00:45:05.980 --> 00:45:07.787
a bunch of experiment stuff and again,

00:45:07.787 --> 00:45:09.890
we didn't really think
of it as a food thing.

00:45:09.890 --> 00:45:11.691
That's all we did.

00:45:11.691 --> 00:45:16.691
The next season, we did
Will It Ice Cream Sandwich

00:45:17.470 --> 00:45:20.544
because in our I'm On Vacation video,

00:45:20.544 --> 00:45:24.840
we played guys who worked in
an ice cream sandwich factory.

00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:27.430
And so we came up with that idea in order

00:45:27.430 --> 00:45:30.101
to promote people
watching our music video.

00:45:30.101 --> 00:45:34.091
And we were like, oh we did
Will It Taco many months earlier

00:45:34.091 --> 00:45:39.091
so May of 2014, let's see.

00:45:40.268 --> 00:45:42.070
June, okay.

00:45:42.070 --> 00:45:43.710
It was only a month later.

00:45:43.710 --> 00:45:46.620
- No it was early, it was
maybe in the beginning

00:45:46.620 --> 00:45:50.250
of season six.
- Yeah so we followed that up.

00:45:50.250 --> 00:45:53.260
And then all of a sudden we
started to do some stuff.

00:45:53.260 --> 00:45:55.110
But again, I can quickly
tell you everything we did

00:45:55.110 --> 00:45:56.860
in season six that was food.

00:45:56.860 --> 00:45:59.190
Smell Tasting, Will It Double Awesome,

00:45:59.190 --> 00:46:00.830
that wasn't food actually.

00:46:00.830 --> 00:46:04.600
Will It Deep Fry and then
we did the Carolina Reaper.

00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:06.930
Did you know that has 25 million views?

00:46:06.930 --> 00:46:08.546
- Yeah that's 'cause a bunch of people--

00:46:08.546 --> 00:46:10.550
- Crazy, man.
- Keep watching it.

00:46:10.550 --> 00:46:12.370
- September of 2014.
- Even now.

00:46:12.370 --> 00:46:14.070
- Guess That Exotic Sausage.

00:46:14.070 --> 00:46:16.160
We did that four episodes later.

00:46:16.160 --> 00:46:18.950
Then we opened the
surstromming with Pewdiepie

00:46:18.950 --> 00:46:20.370
in a Good Mythical More.

00:46:20.370 --> 00:46:22.570
Did Will It Cereal, started
doing a bunch of other Will Its,

00:46:22.570 --> 00:46:23.730
three episodes later we did

00:46:23.730 --> 00:46:26.120
Blind Fast Food Burger Challenge.

00:46:26.120 --> 00:46:27.960
That's when we started
gettin' in the blindfolded

00:46:27.960 --> 00:46:30.495
identifying stuff.

00:46:30.495 --> 00:46:33.848
And we started, you see the slippery slope

00:46:33.848 --> 00:46:38.848
of us starting to eat more
exotic or weird foods.

00:46:39.430 --> 00:46:42.940
It was interesting in my
mind that Will It Taco

00:46:42.940 --> 00:46:44.180
did not click in our minds

00:46:44.180 --> 00:46:46.620
that we were immediately
gonna start doing Will Its.

00:46:46.620 --> 00:46:49.080
Like we do one every month
now but that took a long time

00:46:49.080 --> 00:46:50.780
to get going 'cause the
third one we did was

00:46:50.780 --> 00:46:52.013
Will It Double Awesome.

00:46:52.960 --> 00:46:54.520
'Cause we started doing experiments

00:46:54.520 --> 00:46:56.940
about giving yourself
hiccups so we would start

00:46:56.940 --> 00:46:59.020
to drink a whole bunch of hot sauce.

00:46:59.020 --> 00:47:02.389
We just started to
become much more willing

00:47:02.389 --> 00:47:07.389
to put things down our
throats in order to experiment

00:47:08.040 --> 00:47:08.970
and find stuff out.

00:47:08.970 --> 00:47:12.033
Maybe that's not the best way to put it.

00:47:12.033 --> 00:47:14.840
- Well okay so what we were doing,

00:47:14.840 --> 00:47:18.377
just to put it bluntly, is we were...

00:47:20.280 --> 00:47:24.233
Without even really knowing
or acknowledging at the time,

00:47:26.316 --> 00:47:30.397
we were doing, it was kind
of our personal version

00:47:30.397 --> 00:47:35.397
of what has happened with
the media, with online media.

00:47:35.650 --> 00:47:36.960
- Mm-hmm.
- In general.

00:47:36.960 --> 00:47:40.231
So--
- We became these daredevils

00:47:40.231 --> 00:47:42.710
and we didn't even know it was happening.

00:47:42.710 --> 00:47:44.870
- Well specifically
what I'm saying is that,

00:47:44.870 --> 00:47:49.231
okay so, now the news, the
way that the news works

00:47:49.231 --> 00:47:52.180
is it's based on advertising, right?

00:47:52.180 --> 00:47:53.840
So I mean, I'm not saying anything

00:47:53.840 --> 00:47:56.510
that you don't already
know but basically a lot

00:47:56.510 --> 00:47:58.270
of people are sort of saying

00:47:58.270 --> 00:48:01.320
that journalism is ultimately dead

00:48:01.320 --> 00:48:02.320
if something doesn't change

00:48:02.320 --> 00:48:07.320
because ads are what is
fueling the journalism industry

00:48:08.750 --> 00:48:10.260
and so what do you need?

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:11.840
You need eyeballs.

00:48:11.840 --> 00:48:14.330
Truth is not important,
eyeballs are important.

00:48:14.330 --> 00:48:18.670
So therefore you're going
to title your article

00:48:18.670 --> 00:48:20.010
in a way that gets people to click

00:48:20.010 --> 00:48:22.340
and you're probably gonna
be willing to do something

00:48:22.340 --> 00:48:23.900
that's misleading, right.

00:48:23.900 --> 00:48:26.684
Now we weren't doing, we
were always concerned about

00:48:26.684 --> 00:48:29.756
making sure that when
you clicked on something,

00:48:29.756 --> 00:48:32.140
it wasn't misleading so it's not the same.

00:48:32.140 --> 00:48:34.710
- So we had to actually
put it in our mouths.

00:48:34.710 --> 00:48:37.585
We can't dangle a scorpion
and then not eat it.

00:48:37.585 --> 00:48:39.996
- The news industry has
been completely transformed

00:48:39.996 --> 00:48:41.788
because they want people to click.

00:48:41.788 --> 00:48:45.100
Our lives because we were the ones

00:48:45.100 --> 00:48:47.109
personally putting ourselves
into this situation.

00:48:47.109 --> 00:48:48.910
- Our GI tract.

00:48:48.910 --> 00:48:50.100
- Has been--
- Has been transformed.

00:48:50.100 --> 00:48:52.050
- In fact we were talking
the other day about

00:48:52.050 --> 00:48:54.980
what is the, and this is why
I'm getting my poop analyzed.

